  <title>Browse a backup as a folder</title>
  <desc>Open a whole backup in Files, read only, and copy out what you need.</desc>

  <p>In the <gui>Previous versions</gui> window, <gui style="button">Browse as a folder</gui> opens the backup you chose as an
  ordinary, read-only folder in <app>Files</app>. You can open its files with any application, see thumbnails and
  copy out whatever you need. When you are done, choose <gui style="button">Close the folder</gui>.</p>

  <note style="important">
    <title>A backup cannot be made while one is open</title>
    <p>Opening a backup stops the backup that is running, and Delta resumes it when you close the folder. A scheduled backup
    waits and you are told: <gui>Backup postponed</gui>. The main window says <gui>A backup is open as a folder</gui>.</p>
  </note>

  <section id="closing">
    <title>When the folder closes</title>
    <p>You do not have to remember to close it. Delta closes it when:</p>
    <list>
      <item><p>you choose <gui style="button">Close the folder</gui> or close the <gui>Previous versions</gui> window;</p></item>
      <item><p>the computer suspends or the screen locks;</p></item>
      <item><p>nothing has used it for two to three minutes: no open file, no window showing it. A long copy keeps its file open,
      so it is never cut short.</p></item>
    </list>
    <p>A <app>Files</app> window left on a folder that has just closed shows an error. Close it.</p>
  </section>

  <note style="warning">
    <title>Not in the Flatpak version</title>
    <p>This is only in the native install. A Flatpak cannot make a folder that <app>Files</app> can see, so
    the button is not shown. Everything else works the same.</p>
  </note>
